# The cut files that describe wood which has already been cut.
#
# These were NOT regenerated on 2026-09-09 with the rest of the tree, when
# the sheet was calipered at 2.94mm and the kerf at 0.13mm. They are drawn
# at the old 3.0mm and 0.1mm because they record an instrument that exists.
# repro.py checks them against these hashes instead of redrawing them, so a
# regenerate sweep that overwrites the record fails the gate rather than
# passing every invariant in silence.
#
# 2026-09-13: the twelve pins for fold2-long-straight-3t were REMOVED, on the
# author's instruction to redraw that coil at the current ply and kerf. Its
# record is not lost -- the twelve sheets as cut are in that folder's
# cut-files/old/, and in git before this date -- but its cut-files/ now holds a
# redrawn design, so it is reproduced rather than pinned. Six pins remain, for
# coil-10x10x30-1.5t, which is now the only folder here recording an object.
#
# Rewrite with: repro.py --update -- and only when you have decided to
# overwrite the record, which is what fold2-long-straight/CLAUDE.md asks.
